-- title:
--   Coefficient level field over k₀, q = 2 case
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 2$, let $M' \ge 1$ with $q \nmid M'$, let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and let $\zeta_q \in k_0$ have image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity. Write $F =$ `fieldBar q M'` for the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, inside the Laurent series field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((X))$, of the function field of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$, where $H =$ `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, and regard $k_0$ as a subfield of $F$ through $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. The assertion is that there is an intermediate field $F_0$ of $F/k_0$ with the following four properties. First, an element $f \in F$ lies in $F_0$ precisely when for every $n \in \mathbb{Z}$ the $n$-th Laurent coefficient of $f$ lies in (the image of) $k_0$. Second, the compositum inside $F$ of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the constants $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is all of $F$. Third, $F_0$ is stable under every level automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \subseteq \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$; this is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism of $F$ chosen to satisfy `IsLevelAutBar`, i.e. to transform quotients of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ according to the $\gamma$-translate conjugated at $q$, under any embedding $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \hookrightarrow \mathbb{C}$ sending $\zeta$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$, and to be the identity if no such automorphism exists. Fourth, for every intermediate field $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ that is finite-dimensional over $k_0$, every $m \in \mathbb{N}$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\, m \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ that is $K'$-linearly independent and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\, m \to F$ with each $a_i$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield of $F$ generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ in $F$ forces $a_i = 0$ for all $i$.
--
--   This is the descent datum, in Shimura's sense, of the level field of modular functions whose Fourier coefficients lie in the small constant field $k_0$: the coefficient characterisation, the fact that adjoining all of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ recovers the geometric function field, stability under the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$, and linear disjointness from $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over each finite layer $K'$. It is the $q = 2$ instance, and it feeds the construction of the bottom layer and of the semistable models used in the specialisation arguments for the full-level modular curve.
